<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Go=
od morning Alex! Thanks for joining us today. I'm Sarah, Principal Frontend=
 Engineer here at NAB. Before we dive into the technical discussion, could =
you tell me about your journey as a frontend developer and what attracted y=
ou to this Senior Frontend Engineer role at NAB?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: Good=
 morning Sarah! Thank you for having me. I've been passionate about fronten=
d development for over 6 years now. I started my career working with vanill=
a JavaScript and jQuery, but quickly moved into the React ecosystem when I =
realized its power for building scalable applications.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">What really attracted me to NAB =
is your commitment to <strong>digital transformation in banking</strong> an=
d the scale of your applications. From my research, I understand NAB serves=
 millions of customers, and the frontend engineering challenges around <str=
ong>performance, accessibility, and user experience</strong> at that scale =
are exactly what I'm passionate about solving.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">I've spent the last 3 years at a=
 fintech startup where I led the frontend architecture decisions, implement=
ing React with Next.js, managing complex state with Redux and Zustand, and =
optimizing data fetching with React Query and SWR. The intersection of <str=
ong>financial services and cutting-edge frontend technology</strong> is whe=
re I thrive.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Th=
at's great to hear! At NAB, we definitely face unique challenges with our s=
cale. Can you tell me about a particularly complex frontend challenge you'v=
e solved recently that you're proud of?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: Abso=
lutely! One of the most challenging projects I worked on was rebuilding our=
 trading platform's <strong>real-time dashboard</strong>. We had about 50,0=
00 concurrent users monitoring live market data, and the existing implement=
ation was causing significant performance issues.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The core challenge was <strong>e=
fficiently managing and displaying thousands of rapidly updating data point=
s</strong> without blocking the UI thread. Here's how I approached it:</p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Data Architecture</stro=
ng>: I implemented a hybrid approach using <strong>React Query for server s=
tate</strong> and <strong>Zustand for client state</strong>. React Query ha=
ndled the WebSocket connections and data caching, while Zustand managed UI =
state like filters and user preferences.</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Performance Optimizatio=
n</strong>: I used <strong>React.memo and useMemo extensively</strong> to p=
revent unnecessary re-renders. For the most critical components, I implemen=
ted <strong>virtual scrolling</strong> to handle large datasets efficiently=
.</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Smart Batching</strong>=
: Instead of updating individual components on every WebSocket message, I i=
mplemented a <strong>batching mechanism</strong> that collected updates ove=
r 16ms intervals and applied them in a single render cycle.</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The results were significant: <s=
trong>CPU usage dropped by 60%</strong>, memory consumption reduced by 40%,=
 and we eliminated the UI freezing issues completely. The solution handled =
10x more concurrent data streams than the previous implementation.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Im=
pressive! I can see you understand the performance considerations that are =
crucial for our applications. Let's dive deeper into some technical aspects=
.</p>
