<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>What about handling larg=
e-scale data updates - say 10,000 securities updating simultaneously?</stro=
ng></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: For =
enterprise-scale updates, I'd implement <strong>batched updates with priori=
ty queuing</strong>:</p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Update batching</strong=
>: Collect updates over a time window (e.g., 16ms) and apply them in a sing=
le render cycle</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Priority-based updates<=
/strong>: Update visible rows first, then off-screen data</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Differential updates</s=
trong>: Only update changed fields rather than replacing entire objects</li=
>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Background processing</=
strong>: Use Web Workers for heavy calculations like sorting large datasets=
</li>
</ol>
